# Runtime state (target side) — pi package/skill trees materialized imperatively

# (pi packages on startup, third-party skills by the skills CLI), left in place by

# Apply. First-match wins: ignore each immediate skills-dir child, then re-include

# the authored skills by negation.

.pi/agent/npm/
.pi/agent/git/
.pi/agent/skills/*
!.pi/agent/skills/create-obsidian-reference/**
!.pi/agent/skills/cc-safety-net/**
!.pi/agent/skills/pi-sandbox-runtime/**
!.pi/agent/skills/setup-warden-rules/**

# Guard runtime state (target side) — written by the tools and never managed: warden's
# consent and settings file plus its hold ledger, and the pi-typesafe key store that
# `/typesafe login` writes. The key store is deliberately outside Source so the key is
# never committed; ADR 0004 keeps the fence narrow rather than managing these paths.

.pi/agent/pi-warden/
.pi/agent/pi-typesafe/

# Extension runtime deps (target side) — node_modules materialized by

# run_onchange_after_install-mermaid-lint-deps.sh.tmpl, same source/runtime split as

# the pi package trees.

.pi/agent/extensions/mermaid-lint/node_modules/
.pi/agent/extensions/mermaid-lint/package-lock.json

# Python bytecode (target side) — created when a vendored plugin script is run
# or compiled on the host; never Source state.

**/__pycache__/

